<http://data.silknow.org/object/ca43ceff-9323-3890-9f69-358faf3dae9d/observation/4>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "The closed front of this sack illustrates the typical style of the late 1770s. The combination of stripes and floral motifs is also characteristic of this period. For formal gowns like this one, square-shaped hoops were worn underneath. While most surviving historical costume is small in size, a stout and fairly tall woman wore this particular gown."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/ca43ceff-9323-3890-9f69-358faf3dae9d> .

